examples.question_text:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ contains $A(-3,9)$ and $B(2,-1)$. Find the average rate of change over $[-3,2]$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-4,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3)--(0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.4:2.4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.2*\x*\x-1.8*\x+1.8});
\fill[black] (-3,9) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$A(-3,9)$};
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$B(2,-1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Join $A$ and $B$ with a secant. Moving from $A$ to $B$, the horizontal change is $5$ and the vertical change is $-10$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{secantRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (-4,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3)--(0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.4:2.4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.2*\x*\x-1.8*\x+1.8});
\draw[thick,secantRed] (-3.4,9.8)--(2.4,-1.8);
\draw[dashed,black] (-3,9)--(2,9) node[midway,above] {$\Delta x=5$};
\draw[dashed,black] (2,9)--(2,-1) node[midway,right] {$\Delta y=-10$};
\fill[black] (-3,9) circle (2pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}\text{Average rate}&=\frac{f(2)-f(-3)}{2-(-3)}\\&=\frac{-1-9}{5}\\&=-2\end{aligned}$

examples.question_text:
The graph shows the temperature $T$ ($^{\circ}\text{C}$) of a warming liquid against time $t$ (minutes). Calculate the average rate of temperature change between $t=1.5$ and $t=5$ minutes. Give your answer to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.16cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,32) node[above] {$T$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue] (0,4) .. controls (0.5,6) and (1,9) .. (1.5,11.2) .. controls (2.5,17) and (4,24) .. (5,26.8);
\fill[black] (1.5,11.2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$(1.5,11.2)$};
\fill[black] (5,26.8) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(5,26.8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The straight-line graph shows the volume $V$ (litres) of water remaining in a tank against time $t$ (minutes). Find the rate of change of volume and interpret its sign.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.05cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,100) node[above] {$V$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue] (0,84)--(5,24);
\fill[black] (0,84) circle (2pt) node[right] {$(0,84)$};
\fill[black] (5,24) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$(5,24)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows the total distance $D$ (metres) travelled by an object against time $t$ (seconds). Calculate its average speed between $t=1$ and $t=4$ seconds.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=0.1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(4.8,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,45) node[above] {$D$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=0:4.3,samples=60] plot (\x,{2*\x*\x+\x});
\fill[black] (1,3) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(1,3)$};
\fill[black] (4,36) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(4,36)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
